IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cp6-record-of-earnings`

-- Tests of cp6-record-of-earnings.l4 (sections 95 to 97, lines 2653 to 2676 of the Act file).
-- Expected values are worked out from the text of each section, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- the Record of Earnings`

§§ `Fixtures: four ways of being a contributor, and not being one`

`cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` MEANS `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` WITH
    `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS TRUE
    `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS LIST 0, 0
    `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS FALSE

`cp6 test contributor by self-employed earnings` MEANS `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` WITH
    `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS FALSE
    `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS TRUE
    `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS EMPTY
    `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS FALSE

`cp6 test contributor by a division of earnings` MEANS `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` WITH
    `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS FALSE
    `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS EMPTY
    `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS TRUE

`cp6 test contributor by earnings contributed on in one year` MEANS `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` WITH
    `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS FALSE
    `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS LIST 0, 1500
    `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS FALSE

`cp6 test person who is not a contributor` MEANS `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` WITH
    `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS FALSE
    `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS LIST 0, 0
    `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution`
#ASSERT `a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` `cp6 test contributor by self-employed earnings`
#ASSERT `a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` `cp6 test contributor by a division of earnings`
#ASSERT `a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` `cp6 test contributor by earnings contributed on in one year`
#ASSERT NOT (`a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` `cp6 test person who is not a contributor`)

§§ `Section 95: information is kept in the Record when it is under the Act, about earnings or contributions, and needed for a stated purpose`

-- Inputs in order: obtained under the Act; about earnings and contributions; needed for (a) a benefit; needed for (b) a financial adjustment; needed for (c) identifying earnings from Part I returns.
#ASSERT `s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- A purpose alone is enough (fork C6-F1): the three purposes are alternatives.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Section 96(1): a contributor may require a statement, and ask for reconsideration`

-- Inputs: the facts about the person; the application is in the manner a regulation prescribes; an agreement under section 105 governs.
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test contributor by self-employed earnings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test contributor by a division of earnings` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test contributor by earnings contributed on in one year` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A contributor whose application is not in the prescribed manner has no such claim.
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Someone who is not a contributor has no such claim.
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test person who is not a contributor` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: the section is subject to an agreement under section 105, whose terms are not read here.
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Inputs: the facts; the Minister has furnished a statement; the contributor is not satisfied; an agreement governs.
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement` `cp6 test person who is not a contributor` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement` `cp6 test contributor by an employee's contribution` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 96(2): sections 81 and 82 apply to the request`

#ASSERT `s 96(2) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(2) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` FALSE)

§§ `Section 97(1): four years from the end of the year the entry was made in`

-- An entry made in 2020: the year ends 31 December 2020; four years later is 31 December 2024.
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — the last day on which an entry may be called into question` 2020 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 12 31
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — the last day on which an entry may be called into question` 1999 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2003 12 31
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — the last day on which an entry may be called into question` 2024 EQUALS YearMonthDay 2028 12 31
-- The last day is still open (fork C6-F2); the next day is not.
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1))
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2020 12 31)
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2023 6 15)
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry is conclusively presumed to be accurate on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2025 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry is conclusively presumed to be accurate on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2030 7 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(1) — an entry is conclusively presumed to be accurate on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2024 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(1) — an entry is conclusively presumed to be accurate on a day` 2020 (YearMonthDay 2022 3 1))
-- The following year's entry is open a year longer.
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` 2021 (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30)
#ASSERT `s 97(1) — an entry is conclusively presumed to be accurate on a day` 2021 (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)

§§ `Section 97(2): the Minister may rectify the Record when the amount shown is less than it should be`

-- Inputs: (a) information from an employer's or employee's records after the four years; (b) any other reason; amount shown; amount that should be shown.
#ASSERT `s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` TRUE FALSE 1000 1500
#ASSERT `s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` FALSE TRUE 1000 1500
#ASSERT `s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` TRUE TRUE 0 1
-- Neither source: it does not appear to the Minister that the amount is wrong.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` FALSE FALSE 1000 1500)
-- The amount shown is not less than the amount that should be shown: equal, and more.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` TRUE FALSE 1500 1500)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` TRUE TRUE 1600 1500)

§§ `Section 97(2.1): removal of an entry that is really a provincial plan contribution`

-- Inputs: furnished under an agreement referred to in paragraph 105(a); it appears to the Minister; the day the information was furnished; the day.
#ASSERT `s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10)
#ASSERT `s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2031 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 9))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day` FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2025 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1))

§§ `Section 97(3): another contributor's earnings may be reduced`

#ASSERT `s 97(3) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified by a reduction of another contributor's earnings` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(3) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified by a reduction of another contributor's earnings` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(3) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified by a reduction of another contributor's earnings` FALSE TRUE)
-- 12,000 shown to the other contributor; 2,500 of the increase was incorrectly shown there: 12,000 less 2,500 is 9,500.
#ASSERT `s 97(3) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor after any reduction` TRUE 12000 2500 EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `s 97(3) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor after any reduction` FALSE 12000 2500 EQUALS 12000

§§ `Section 97(4): notice of a reduction, and reconsideration of it`

-- Inputs: a reduction is made; the Record shows the contributor was informed under section 96.
#ASSERT `s 97(4) — the Minister must notify the contributor of the reduction` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — the Minister must notify the contributor of the reduction` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — the Minister must notify the contributor of the reduction` FALSE TRUE)
-- Regulation 40: in writing at the latest known address.
#ASSERT `s 97(4) — the notice of the reduction was given in the prescribed manner` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — the notice of the reduction was given in the prescribed manner` FALSE)
-- Inputs: a reduction is made; informed under section 96; the contributor is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 97(4) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the reduction` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the reduction` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the reduction` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the reduction` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 97(4) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 97(4) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` FALSE)
